<title>USA: Checkpoint Systems Q1 shr $0.07 vs $0.10.</title>
<headline>Checkpoint Systems Q1 shr $0.07 vs $0.10.</headline>
<dateline>THOROFARE, N.J. 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Checkpoint Systems, Inc.</p>
<p>			 (Thousands, except per share data)</p>
<p>				    Quarter (13 Weeks) Ended</p>
<p>				     Mar 30,	  Mar 31,</p>
<p>					  1997	     1996</p>
<p> Net revenues		   $ 68,178	 $ 66,994</p>
<p> Cost of revenues		 40,141	   39,556</p>
<p>   Gross profit		   28,037	   27,438</p>
<p>Selling, general and</p>
<p>  administrative expenses     26,697	   22,259</p>
<p> Income from operations	  1,340	    5,179</p>
<p> Interest income		   2,831	    1,019</p>
<p> Interest expense		  2,449	    2,343</p>
<p> Other income			1,888		478</p>
<p> Income before income taxes    3,610	    4,333</p>
<p> Income taxes			1,175	    1,387</p>
<p> Net earnings			2,435	    2,946</p>
<p> Net earnings per share	    .07		.10</p>
<p>Weighted average number</p>
<p>of common and common</p>
<p>  equivalent shares	     36,108	   30,957</p>
<p>NOTE:  First quarter 1997 results include a one time, non-recurring expense of approximately $1,500,000 or three cents per share related to the terminated Ultrak merger.  Also during the first quarter, the company received a $1,300,000 payment from Mitsubishi Materials Corporation for the establishment of a joint product research and development project solely dedicated to developing radio frequency intelligent tagging solutions for retail and library applications.</p>
